<DynamicFolderExport>
  <Name>Dynamic Folder Export</Name>
  <Objects>
    <DynamicFolderExportObject>
      <Type>DynamicFolder</Type>
      <Name>Azure VM (PowerShell)</Name>
      <Description>Starts one Azure VM if needed, resolves its current IP address, and generates selected RDP, password-based SSH, and Azure AD-based AzSSH connections.</Description>
      <Notes><![CDATA[<h2>Microsoft Azure VM Dynamic Folder</h2>
<p><strong>Version:</strong> 1.0.0<br />
<strong>Author:</strong> Ghost93</p>
<p>This sample generates connection objects for one Azure virtual machine. Duplicate the imported
Dynamic Folder for additional VMs and change only its Custom Properties. The wrapper embeds a
PowerShell 7 script inline; when the Dynamic Folder reloads, the wrapper writes it to a temporary
file, invokes it with <code>pwsh.exe</code>, then deletes the temporary file.</p>
<p>Azure AD SSH uses the Windows Custom Terminal PTY support requested in
<a href="https://github.com/royalapplications/toolbox/issues/141">toolbox issue #141</a>.</p>
<h3>Prerequisites</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Windows and Royal TS 26 or newer.</li>
  <li>PowerShell 7 with the Az module: <code>Install-Module Az -Scope CurrentUser</code>.</li>
  <li>A cached PowerShell Azure session created with <code>Connect-AzAccount</code>.</li>
  <li>For AzSSH, Azure CLI with SSH extension 2.0.4 or newer and a cached <code>az login</code> session.</li>
  <li>Royal TS credentials matching <strong>CredentialName</strong> for RDP and
  <strong>SshCredentialName</strong> for password-based SSH.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Setup</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Import this <code>.rdfx</code> into Royal TS. The PowerShell 7 script that queries Azure is
  embedded inside the wrapper; no additional file needs to be downloaded.</li>
  <li>Set <strong>SubscriptionId</strong>, <strong>ResourceGroup</strong>, <strong>VmName</strong>,
  <strong>ConnectionName</strong>, credential names, <strong>IpType</strong>, and
  <strong>Protocols</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Protocols</strong> accepts <code>RDP</code>, <code>SSH</code>, <code>AzSSH</code>,
  or comma-separated combinations such as <code>RDP,SSH,AzSSH</code>.</li>
  <li>Optional: set <strong>StartVm</strong> to <code>true</code> to auto-start a stopped VM when the
  Dynamic Folder reloads. Default is <code>false</code>; if the VM is stopped, the reload fails with
  a visible error rather than silently starting the VM and incurring Azure cost.</li>
  <li>Reload the Dynamic Folder.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Behavior</h3>
<ul>
  <li>When <strong>StartVm</strong> is <code>true</code>, the script starts a stopped VM, waits
  for provisioning and network readiness, then emits deterministic RoyalJSON connection IDs. When
  <strong>StartVm</strong> is <code>false</code> and the VM is stopped, the reload fails; start
  the VM manually or set <strong>StartVm</strong> to <code>true</code>.</li>
  <li>RDP and SSH reference Royal TS credentials by name. No password or private key is emitted.</li>
  <li>AzSSH starts an embedded Custom Terminal and runs <code>az ssh vm</code> with a forced TTY
  and Bash login shell. Azure CLI performs the Azure AD authentication.</li>
  <li>Public RDP or SSH requires the VM's network security group to permit the selected port from
  the Royal TS client.</li>
  <li>Diagnostics are written to <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\RoyalTS\AzureVmDynamicFolder\logs\Get-AzureVmConnections.log</code> with a cross-process lock.</li>
</ul>]]></Notes>
      <CustomProperties>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>SubscriptionId</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>ResourceGroup</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>my-resource-group</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>VmName</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>my-azure-vm</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>ConnectionName</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>My Azure VM</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>CredentialName</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>Windows VM Credential</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>SshCredentialName</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>Linux VM Credential</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>IpType</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>Public</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>Protocols</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>RDP,SSH,AzSSH</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>StartVm</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>false</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
        <CustomProperty>
          <Name>SshPort</Name>
          <Type>Text</Type>
          <Value>22</Value>
        </CustomProperty>
      </CustomProperties>
      <ScriptInterpreter>powershell</ScriptInterpreter>
      <Script><![CDATA[# Wrapper runs under Windows PowerShell 5.1 (Royal TS default).
# Explicitly invoke PS7 so the Az module is available, and bypass execution policy for the target script.
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'

# Text Custom Properties are single-line values. Literal here-strings keep quotes and PowerShell
# metacharacters in those values from becoming wrapper code.
function ConvertFrom-RoyalText {
    param([string]$Value)

    $resolvedValue = $Value.TrimEnd([char[]]"`r`n")
    if (
        $resolvedValue.StartsWith('$') -and
        $resolvedValue.EndsWith('$') -and
        $resolvedValue.Contains('CustomProperty.')
    ) {
        throw "A required Dynamic Folder Custom Property could not be resolved."
    }

    return $resolvedValue
}

$subscriptionId = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.SubscriptionId$
'@
$resourceGroup = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.ResourceGroup$
'@
$vmName = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.VmName$
'@
$connectionName = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.ConnectionName$
'@
$credentialName = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.CredentialName$
'@
$sshCredentialName = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.SshCredentialName$
'@
$protocols = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.Protocols$
'@
$sshPort = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.SshPort$
'@
$ipType = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.IpType$
'@
$startVm = ConvertFrom-RoyalText @'
$CustomProperty.StartVm$
'@
$startVmValue = $startVm.Trim()
if ($startVmValue -notmatch '^(true|false)$') {
    throw "StartVm must be either 'true' or 'false'."
}

$pwshCommand = Get-Command pwsh.exe -CommandType Application -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
    Select-Object -First 1
$pwsh = if ($pwshCommand) {
    $pwshCommand.Source
} else {
    Join-Path $env:ProgramFiles 'PowerShell\7\pwsh.exe'
}

if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $pwsh -PathType Leaf)) {
    throw "PowerShell 7 executable was not found. Expected 'pwsh.exe' on PATH or at '$pwsh'."
}

# The full PowerShell 7 worker script is embedded below as a single-quoted here-string
# so that no external file is required. It is written to a temp .ps1 file and invoked via
# 'pwsh.exe -File' so that PS7 parameter binding and $PSScriptRoot resolution work correctly.
$embeddedScript = @'
<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Emits Royal TS connections for an Azure VM as RoyalJSON.

.DESCRIPTION
    On reload, this script:
      1. Validates its Dynamic Folder parameters.
      2. Selects the Azure subscription in process scope.
      3. Starts the VM when requested and waits for it to reach the running state.
      4. Resolves the selected primary or named NIC and IP configuration.
      5. Waits for every selected protocol port when a wait timeout is configured.
      6. Emits stable RDP, local SSH, and Azure AD SSH RoyalJSON objects.

    RDP and local SSH connections reference Royal TS credentials by name. Azure AD SSH uses a
    Royal TS 26 Custom Terminal that starts the VM, invokes Azure CLI SSH, forces a remote TTY,
    and opens a Bash login shell.

.NOTES
    Royal TS Dynamic Folders require valid rJSON on stdout and exit code 0. All diagnostics are
    written to the optional log file or stderr.
#>

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    # Azure target
    [string]$SubscriptionId = '<YOUR-SUBSCRIPTION-ID>',
    [string]$ResourceGroup = '<YOUR-RESOURCE-GROUP>',
    [string]$VmName = '<YOUR-VM-NAME>',
    [string]$NetworkInterfaceName = '',
    [string]$IpConfigurationName = '',

    # Royal TS presentation and credentials
    [string]$ConnectionName = 'Azure VM',
    [string]$CredentialName = 'Azure VM',
    [string]$SshCredentialName = '',
    [ValidateRange(1, 65535)]
    [int]$RdpPort = 3389,
    [ValidateRange(1, 65535)]
    [int]$SshPort = 22,

    # Protocols and addressing
    [string]$Protocols = 'RDP',
    [ValidateSet('Public', 'Private')]
    [string]$IpType = 'Public',

    # Azure AD SSH Custom Terminal
    [string]$AzSshRemoteShell = '/usr/bin/bash',
    [string]$AzSshTerm = 'xterm-256color',
    [string]$AzSshColorTerm = 'truecolor',
    [string]$AzSshFont = 'Consolas',
    [ValidateRange(6, 72)]
    [int]$AzSshFontSize = 10,

    # Runtime behavior
    [switch]$StartIfStopped,
    [ValidateRange(30, 1800)]
    [int]$VmStartTimeoutSeconds = 300,
    [ValidateRange(0, 600)]
    [int]$AddressWaitSeconds = 60,
    [ValidateRange(0, 600)]
    [int]$PortWaitSeconds = 60,
    [ValidateRange(1, 30)]
    [int]$PollIntervalSeconds = 3,
    [string]$LogPath = (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'logs\Get-AzureVmConnections.log'),
    [switch]$DisableFileLogging,

    # Test mode
    [string]$TestModeAddress = '10.0.0.4',
    [switch]$TestMode
)

if ($DisableFileLogging) {
    $LogPath = ''
}

$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$WarningPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'
$ProgressPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'
$VerbosePreference = 'SilentlyContinue'
$InformationPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'
$env:SuppressAzurePowerShellBreakingChangeWarnings = 'true'

function Initialize-Log {
    Write-Log -Level INFO -Message 'Log initialized.'
}

function Write-Log {
    param(
        [ValidateSet('DEBUG', 'INFO', 'WARN', 'ERROR')]
        [string]$Level,
        [string]$Message
    )

    if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($LogPath)) {
        return
    }

    $line = "$(Get-Date -Format o) [$Level] $Message$([Environment]::NewLine)"
    $normalizedLogPath = [System.IO.Path]::GetFullPath($LogPath).ToUpperInvariant()
    $lockId = New-DeterministicGuid -Value $normalizedLogPath

    try {
        Invoke-WithNamedMutex `
            -Name "Local\RoyalTS-Log-$lockId" `
            -WaitSeconds 10 `
            -ScriptBlock {
                $logDirectory = Split-Path -Parent $LogPath
                if ($logDirectory -and -not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $logDirectory)) {
                    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $logDirectory -Force | Out-Null
                }

                [System.IO.File]::AppendAllText(
                    $LogPath,
                    $line,
                    [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false)
                )
            }
    } catch {
        [Console]::Error.WriteLine("Logging failed for '$LogPath': $($_.Exception.Message)")
    }
}

function Resolve-SelectedProtocols {
    param([string]$Value)

    $allowed = @('RDP', 'SSH', 'AZSSH')
    $tokens = @(
        $Value -split '[,;\s]+' |
            Where-Object { -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($_) } |
            ForEach-Object { $_.Trim().ToUpperInvariant() }
    )

    if ($tokens.Count -eq 0) {
        throw 'Protocols cannot be empty.'
    }

    $invalid = @($tokens | Where-Object { $_ -notin $allowed } | Select-Object -Unique)
    if ($invalid.Count -gt 0) {
        throw "Unsupported protocol value(s): $($invalid -join ', '). Allowed values: RDP, SSH, AzSSH."
    }

    $selected = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()
    foreach ($token in $tokens) {
        if (-not $selected.Contains($token)) {
            $selected.Add($token)
        }
    }

    return $selected.ToArray()
}

function Assert-RequiredParameters {
    foreach ($parameter in @(
        @{ Name = 'SubscriptionId'; Value = $SubscriptionId },
        @{ Name = 'ResourceGroup'; Value = $ResourceGroup },
        @{ Name = 'VmName'; Value = $VmName },
        @{ Name = 'ConnectionName'; Value = $ConnectionName }
    )) {
        if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($parameter.Value) -or $parameter.Value -like '<*>') {
            throw "Missing required parameter -$($parameter.Name)."
        }
    }

    if ($CredentialName -like '<*>') {
        throw 'CredentialName still contains a placeholder value.'
    }
}

function New-DeterministicGuid {
    param([string]$Value)

    $inputBytes = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($Value)
    $hash = [System.Security.Cryptography.SHA256]::HashData($inputBytes)
    $guidBytes = [byte[]]::new(16)
    [System.Array]::Copy($hash, $guidBytes, 16)

    # Mark the value as an RFC 4122-compatible version 5-style GUID.
    $guidBytes[7] = ($guidBytes[7] -band 0x0F) -bor 0x50
    $guidBytes[8] = ($guidBytes[8] -band 0x3F) -bor 0x80
    return [guid]::new($guidBytes).ToString()
}

function Get-ConnectionId {
    param([string]$Protocol)

    $identityProtocol = if ($Protocol -eq 'AZSSH') {
        'AZSSH-CUSTOMTERMINAL-V6'
    } else {
        $Protocol
    }

    return New-DeterministicGuid -Value "$SubscriptionId|$ResourceGroup|$VmName|$identityProtocol"
}

function Get-ArmResourceIdSegment {
    param(
        [string]$ResourceId,
        [string]$SegmentName
    )

    $segments = $ResourceId.Trim('/') -split '/'
    for ($index = 0; $index -lt $segments.Count - 1; $index++) {
        if ($segments[$index] -ieq $SegmentName) {
            return $segments[$index + 1]
        }
    }

    throw "ARM resource ID '$ResourceId' does not contain segment '$SegmentName'."
}

function Get-EffectiveSshCredentialName {
    if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($SshCredentialName)) {
        return $CredentialName
    }

    return $SshCredentialName
}

function ConvertTo-CmdQuotedArgument {
    param(
        [string]$Value,
        [string]$Name
    )

    if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($Value)) {
        throw "$Name cannot be empty."
    }
    if ($Value.IndexOfAny([char[]]"`r`n`"") -ge 0) {
        throw "$Name contains unsupported command-line characters."
    }

    return "`"$Value`""
}

function Assert-AzSshPrerequisites {
    if (-not (Get-Command az -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) {
        throw "Azure CLI executable 'az' was not found. Install Azure CLI and sign in with 'az login'."
    }

    foreach ($terminalValue in @(
        @{ Name = 'AzSshTerm'; Value = $AzSshTerm },
        @{ Name = 'AzSshColorTerm'; Value = $AzSshColorTerm }
    )) {
        if ($terminalValue.Value -notmatch '^[A-Za-z0-9._+-]+$') {
            throw "$($terminalValue.Name) contains unsupported characters."
        }
    }
}

function New-AzSshCustomCommand {
    $resourceGroupArgument = ConvertTo-CmdQuotedArgument -Value $ResourceGroup -Name 'ResourceGroup'
    $vmNameArgument = ConvertTo-CmdQuotedArgument -Value $VmName -Name 'VmName'
    $subscriptionArgument = ConvertTo-CmdQuotedArgument -Value $SubscriptionId -Name 'SubscriptionId'
    $remoteShellArgument = ConvertTo-CmdQuotedArgument -Value $AzSshRemoteShell -Name 'AzSshRemoteShell'
    $termArgument = ConvertTo-CmdQuotedArgument -Value "TERM=$AzSshTerm" -Name 'AzSshTerm'
    $colorTermArgument = ConvertTo-CmdQuotedArgument -Value "COLORTERM=$AzSshColorTerm" -Name 'AzSshColorTerm'

    $targetArguments = "-g $resourceGroupArgument -n $vmNameArgument --subscription $subscriptionArgument"
    $commands = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()

    if ($StartIfStopped) {
        $commands.Add("az vm start $targetArguments --only-show-errors")
    }

    $sshCommand = "az ssh vm $targetArguments --resource-type Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines --port $SshPort --only-show-errors"
    if ($IpType -eq 'Private') {
        $sshCommand += ' --prefer-private-ip'
    }
    $sshCommand += " -- -tt `"/usr/bin/env`" $termArgument $colorTermArgument $remoteShellArgument --login"
    $commands.Add($sshCommand)

    return "cmd.exe /d /k $($commands -join ' && ')"
}

function Get-VmPowerState {
    param($Context)

    $vm = Get-AzVM `
        -ResourceGroupName $ResourceGroup `
        -Name $VmName `
        -Status `
        -DefaultProfile $Context

    $statuses = @($vm.Statuses)
    $state = ($statuses | Where-Object { $_.Code -like 'PowerState/*' } | Select-Object -First 1).Code
    if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($state)) {
        return $state
    }

    $provisioningFailure = $statuses |
        Where-Object {
            $_.Code -like 'ProvisioningState/failed*' -or
            $_.DisplayStatus -eq 'Provisioning failed'
        } |
        Select-Object -First 1
    if ($provisioningFailure) {
        $details = @(
            $provisioningFailure.Code,
            $provisioningFailure.Message
        ) | Where-Object { -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($_) }
        throw "Azure provisioning failed for VM '$VmName': $($details -join ' - ')"
    }

    return $null
}

function Ensure-AzureVmRunning {
    param($Context)

    $deadline = (Get-Date).AddSeconds($VmStartTimeoutSeconds)
    $startRequested = $false
    $lastState = ''
    $missingStateLogged = $false

    do {
        $state = Get-VmPowerState -Context $Context
        if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($state)) {
            if (-not $missingStateLogged) {
                Write-Log -Level WARN -Message "Azure did not return a power state for VM '$VmName'; retrying."
                $missingStateLogged = $true
            }
            Start-Sleep -Seconds $PollIntervalSeconds
            continue
        }

        $missingStateLogged = $false
        if ($state -ne $lastState) {
            Write-Log -Level INFO -Message "VM '$VmName' power state: $state"
            $lastState = $state
        }

        switch ($state) {
            'PowerState/running' {
                return
            }
            { $_ -in @('PowerState/stopped', 'PowerState/deallocated') } {
                if (-not $StartIfStopped) {
                    throw "VM '$VmName' is '$state' and StartIfStopped is disabled."
                }

                if (-not $startRequested) {
                    Write-Log -Level INFO -Message "Starting VM '$VmName'."
                    Start-AzVM `
                        -ResourceGroupName $ResourceGroup `
                        -Name $VmName `
                        -NoWait `
                        -DefaultProfile $Context | Out-Null
                    $startRequested = $true
                }
            }
            { $_ -in @('PowerState/starting', 'PowerState/stopping', 'PowerState/deallocating') } {
                # Wait for the transition to complete.
            }
            default {
                throw "VM '$VmName' is in unsupported power state '$state'."
            }
        }

        Start-Sleep -Seconds $PollIntervalSeconds
    } while ((Get-Date) -lt $deadline)

    throw "VM '$VmName' did not reach PowerState/running within $VmStartTimeoutSeconds seconds. Last state: $lastState."
}

function Select-NetworkInterfaceReference {
    param($VmModel)

    $references = @($VmModel.NetworkProfile.NetworkInterfaces)
    if ($references.Count -eq 0) {
        throw "VM '$VmName' has no network interfaces."
    }

    if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($NetworkInterfaceName)) {
        $match = $references |
            Where-Object { (Split-Path -Leaf $_.Id) -eq $NetworkInterfaceName } |
            Select-Object -First 1
        if (-not $match) {
            throw "Network interface '$NetworkInterfaceName' is not attached to VM '$VmName'."
        }
        return $match
    }

    $primary = $references | Where-Object { $_.Primary } | Select-Object -First 1
    if ($primary) {
        return $primary
    }

    Write-Log -Level WARN -Message "No primary NIC was marked for '$VmName'; using '$((Split-Path -Leaf $references[0].Id))'."
    return $references[0]
}

function Select-IpConfiguration {
    param($NetworkInterface)

    $configurations = @($NetworkInterface.IpConfigurations)
    if ($configurations.Count -eq 0) {
        throw "Network interface '$($NetworkInterface.Name)' has no IP configurations."
    }

    if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($IpConfigurationName)) {
        $match = $configurations | Where-Object { $_.Name -eq $IpConfigurationName } | Select-Object -First 1
        if (-not $match) {
            throw "IP configuration '$IpConfigurationName' was not found on NIC '$($NetworkInterface.Name)'."
        }
        return $match
    }

    $primary = $configurations | Where-Object { $_.Primary } | Select-Object -First 1
    if ($primary) {
        return $primary
    }

    Write-Log -Level WARN -Message "No primary IP configuration was marked on '$($NetworkInterface.Name)'; using '$($configurations[0].Name)'."
    return $configurations[0]
}

function Get-AzureVmAddress {
    param($Context)

    $deadline = (Get-Date).AddSeconds($AddressWaitSeconds)

    do {
        $vmModel = Get-AzVM `
            -ResourceGroupName $ResourceGroup `
            -Name $VmName `
            -DefaultProfile $Context

        $nicReference = Select-NetworkInterfaceReference -VmModel $vmModel
        $networkInterface = Get-AzNetworkInterface -ResourceId $nicReference.Id -DefaultProfile $Context
        $ipConfiguration = Select-IpConfiguration -NetworkInterface $networkInterface

        if ($IpType -eq 'Private') {
            $address = $ipConfiguration.PrivateIpAddress
        } elseif ($ipConfiguration.PublicIpAddress) {
            $publicIpResourceId = $ipConfiguration.PublicIpAddress.Id
            $publicIpResourceGroup = Get-ArmResourceIdSegment `
                -ResourceId $publicIpResourceId `
                -SegmentName 'resourceGroups'
            $publicIpName = Split-Path -Leaf $publicIpResourceId
            $publicIp = Get-AzPublicIpAddress `
                -ResourceGroupName $publicIpResourceGroup `
                -Name $publicIpName `
                -DefaultProfile $Context
            $address = $publicIp.IpAddress
        } else {
            throw "IP configuration '$($ipConfiguration.Name)' on VM '$VmName' has no public IP resource."
        }

        if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($address) -and $address -ne 'Not Assigned') {
            Write-Log -Level INFO -Message "Resolved $IpType IP '$address' from NIC '$($networkInterface.Name)' and IP configuration '$($ipConfiguration.Name)'."
            return $address
        }

        if ($AddressWaitSeconds -eq 0) {
            break
        }

        Start-Sleep -Seconds $PollIntervalSeconds
    } while ((Get-Date) -lt $deadline)

    throw "Could not resolve a usable $IpType IP for VM '$VmName' within $AddressWaitSeconds seconds."
}

function Invoke-WithNamedMutex {
    param(
        [string]$Name,
        [int]$WaitSeconds = 120,
        [scriptblock]$ScriptBlock
    )

    $mutex = [System.Threading.Mutex]::new($false, $Name)
    $acquired = $false

    try {
        try {
            $acquired = $mutex.WaitOne([TimeSpan]::FromSeconds($WaitSeconds))
        } catch [System.Threading.AbandonedMutexException] {
            $acquired = $true
        }

        if (-not $acquired) {
            throw "Timed out after $WaitSeconds seconds waiting for lock '$Name'."
        }

        return & $ScriptBlock
    } finally {
        if ($acquired) {
            $mutex.ReleaseMutex()
        }
        $mutex.Dispose()
    }
}

function Test-TcpPort {
    param(
        [string]$ComputerName,
        [int]$Port
    )

    $client = [System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient]::new()
    try {
        $connectTask = $client.ConnectAsync($ComputerName, $Port)
        if (-not $connectTask.Wait(1000)) {
            return $false
        }
        return $client.Connected
    } catch {
        return $false
    } finally {
        $client.Dispose()
    }
}

function Wait-ConnectionPorts {
    param(
        [string]$ComputerName,
        [string[]]$SelectedProtocols
    )

    if ($PortWaitSeconds -eq 0) {
        return
    }

    $requiredPorts = [System.Collections.Generic.HashSet[int]]::new()
    foreach ($protocol in $SelectedProtocols) {
        if ($protocol -eq 'RDP') {
            [void]$requiredPorts.Add($RdpPort)
        } else {
            [void]$requiredPorts.Add($SshPort)
        }
    }

    $deadline = (Get-Date).AddSeconds($PortWaitSeconds)
    $unavailablePorts = @()

    do {
        $unavailablePorts = @(
            foreach ($port in $requiredPorts) {
                if (-not (Test-TcpPort -ComputerName $ComputerName -Port $port)) {
                    $port
                }
            }
        )

        if ($unavailablePorts.Count -eq 0) {
            Write-Log -Level INFO -Message "Required connection ports are available: $($requiredPorts -join ', ')."
            return
        }

        Start-Sleep -Seconds $PollIntervalSeconds
    } while ((Get-Date) -lt $deadline)

    throw "Port readiness timed out after $PortWaitSeconds seconds for '$ComputerName'. Unavailable port(s): $($unavailablePorts -join ', ')."
}

function New-RoyalJsonDocument {
    param(
        [string]$ComputerName,
        [string[]]$SelectedProtocols
    )

    $multipleProtocols = $SelectedProtocols.Count -gt 1
    $generatedAt = Get-Date -Format s
    $objects = [System.Collections.Generic.List[object]]::new()

    foreach ($protocol in $SelectedProtocols) {
        $name = if ($multipleProtocols) { "$ConnectionName ($protocol)" } else { $ConnectionName }

        switch ($protocol) {
            'RDP' {
                $objects.Add([ordered]@{
                    Type = 'RemoteDesktopConnection'
                    ID = Get-ConnectionId -Protocol $protocol
                    Name = $name
                    ComputerName = $ComputerName
                    Port = $RdpPort
                    CredentialName = $CredentialName
                    Description = "Azure VM $VmName ($ResourceGroup) - RDP - generated $generatedAt"
                })
            }
            'SSH' {
                $objects.Add([ordered]@{
                    Type = 'TerminalConnection'
                    ID = Get-ConnectionId -Protocol $protocol
                    TerminalConnectionType = 'SSH'
                    Name = $name
                    ComputerName = $ComputerName
                    Port = $SshPort
                    CredentialName = Get-EffectiveSshCredentialName
                    Description = "Azure VM $VmName ($ResourceGroup) - local SSH - generated $generatedAt"
                })
            }
            'AZSSH' {
                $objects.Add([ordered]@{
                    Type = 'TerminalConnection'
                    ID = Get-ConnectionId -Protocol $protocol
                    TerminalConnectionType = 'CustomTerminal'
                    Name = $name
                    ComputerName = $ComputerName
                    CredentialMode = 0
                    CredentialAutologon = $false
                    CredentialFromParent = $false
                    Properties = [ordered]@{
                        CustomCommandWin = New-AzSshCustomCommand
                        Font = $AzSshFont
                        FontSize = "$AzSshFontSize"
                    }
                    Description = "Azure VM $VmName ($ResourceGroup) - Azure AD SSH via Custom Terminal - generated $generatedAt"
                })
            }
        }
    }

    return [ordered]@{ Objects = $objects.ToArray() } | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 10
}

try {
    Initialize-Log
    $selectedProtocols = Resolve-SelectedProtocols -Value $Protocols
    Write-Log -Level INFO -Message "Reload started for '$ResourceGroup/$VmName' with protocols '$($selectedProtocols -join ',')'."

    if ($TestMode) {
        $testJson = New-RoyalJsonDocument `
            -ComputerName $TestModeAddress `
            -SelectedProtocols $selectedProtocols
        [Console]::Out.WriteLine($testJson)
        Write-Log -Level INFO -Message 'Test mode reload completed.'
        exit 0
    }

    Assert-RequiredParameters
    if ($selectedProtocols -contains 'AZSSH') {
        Assert-AzSshPrerequisites
    }

    $currentContext = Get-AzContext -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    if (-not $currentContext) {
        throw "No Az PowerShell context found. Run 'Connect-AzAccount' in PowerShell 7, then reload this folder."
    }

    $context = Set-AzContext -Subscription $SubscriptionId -Scope Process
    Write-Log -Level INFO -Message "Selected Azure subscription '$($context.Subscription.Id)' in process scope."

    Ensure-AzureVmRunning -Context $context
    $address = Get-AzureVmAddress -Context $context

    Wait-ConnectionPorts -ComputerName $address -SelectedProtocols $selectedProtocols

    $json = New-RoyalJsonDocument `
        -ComputerName $address `
        -SelectedProtocols $selectedProtocols

    [Console]::Out.WriteLine($json)
    Write-Log -Level INFO -Message 'Reload completed successfully.'
    exit 0
} catch {
    $message = "Dynamic Folder script failed: $($_.Exception.Message)"
    $loggingFailure = $null
    try {
        Write-Log -Level ERROR -Message $message
    } catch {
        $loggingFailure = $_.Exception.Message
    }

    [Console]::Error.WriteLine($message)
    if ($loggingFailure) {
        [Console]::Error.WriteLine("Additionally, logging failed: $loggingFailure")
    }
    exit 1
}
'@

$tempScript = Join-Path ([System.IO.Path]::GetTempPath()) ("royalts-azurevm-" + [Guid]::NewGuid().ToString() + ".ps1")
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($tempScript, $embeddedScript, (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)))

try {
    $arguments = @(
        '-ExecutionPolicy', 'Bypass',
        '-NonInteractive',
        '-File', $tempScript,
        '-SubscriptionId', $subscriptionId,
        '-ResourceGroup', $resourceGroup,
        '-VmName', $vmName,
        '-ConnectionName', $connectionName,
        '-CredentialName', $credentialName,
        '-SshCredentialName', $sshCredentialName,
        '-Protocols', $protocols,
        '-SshPort', $sshPort,
        '-IpType', $ipType,
        '-LogPath', (Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'RoyalTS\AzureVmDynamicFolder\logs\Get-AzureVmConnections.log')
    )
    if ($startVmValue -ieq 'true') {
        $arguments += '-StartIfStopped'
    }

    & $pwsh @arguments
    $exitCode = $LASTEXITCODE
    if ($null -eq $exitCode) {
        throw "PowerShell 7 exited without reporting a process exit code."
    }

    exit $exitCode
}
finally {
    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $tempScript) {
        Remove-Item -LiteralPath $tempScript -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    }
}]]></Script>
      <DynamicCredentialScriptInterpreter>json</DynamicCredentialScriptInterpreter>
    </DynamicFolderExportObject>
  </Objects>
</DynamicFolderExport>
